  "lineage": "Rural Jamaican work songs sung by digging and planting gangs, a leader raising a line and the group answering in time with the strokes of their tools, together with the ring-play (ring-game) songs sung and clapped in circle games. Louise Bennett recorded a selection of Jamaican folk songs for Folkways in the 1950s, and the African-Caribbean Institute of Jamaica holds field recordings.",
